# Citation metadata for the structured entries dataset published by this
# repository. GitHub renders this as the "Cite this repository" button.
#
# Scope note: `license: CC0-1.0` applies to the extracted entries data (the
# CSVs and their derivatives), which is also published at
# https://huggingface.co/datasets/hadro/green-books-travel-guides. Third-party
# components vendored here keep their own licenses — notably
# `clover.umd-*.js` (Clover IIIF, MIT), `vendor/` (Leaflet and
# Leaflet.markercluster, BSD-2-Clause / MIT), and
# `nyc-neighborhoods/nyc-neighborhoods*.geojson` (CC BY-SA 4.0, see
# `nyc-neighborhoods/README.md`). The digitized page images remain with their
# holding institutions.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "Green Books & Black Travel Guides: Structured Entries from 50 Digitized African American Travel Guides, 1930–1966"
abstract: >-
  A structured dataset of 113,827 business listings transcribed from 50
  digitized volumes of eight African American travel guides published between
  1930 and 1966, including all 24 known editions of The Negro Motorist Green
  Book. Each entry records the business name, street address, city, state,
  category, proprietor and telephone where printed, the publication and edition
  year, and a IIIF canvas URI locating the listing on the scanned page it came
  from. The entries were produced by OCR and large-language-model extraction
  over page scans held by the New York Public Library's Schomburg Center for
  Research in Black Culture, with the 1946 Green Book edition digitized by the
  Library of Congress. As machine-extracted historical text, the data contains
  transcription errors and should be checked against the linked page image for
  any use where exactness matters.
authors:
  - family-names: Hadro
    given-names: Josh
    alias: hadro
repository-code: "https://github.com/hadro/green-books"
url: "https://hadro.github.io/green-books/all-volumes"
license: CC0-1.0
keywords:
  - Green Book
  - The Negro Motorist Green Book
  - African American travel guides
  - Black travel
  - Jim Crow
  - segregation
  - Black-owned businesses
  - historical business directories
  - African American history
  - IIIF
  - cultural heritage
  - digital humanities
references:
  - type: database
    title: "Green Books & Black Travel Guides — combined entries dataset"
    authors:
      - family-names: Hadro
        given-names: Josh
    url: "https://huggingface.co/datasets/hadro/green-books-travel-guides"
    license: CC0-1.0
  - type: software
    title: "directory-pipeline — the OCR and entity-extraction pipeline that produced this data"
    authors:
